<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Go-Kameyama</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1424</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Go-Kameyama (died 1424) was the fourth and last emperor of the Southern Court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, reigning from 1383 to 1392. Militarily weakened, he accepted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogun</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashikaga-yoshimitsu">Ashikaga Yoshimitsu</a>'s offer to reunite the two courts, handing the imperial regalia to the Northern emperor Go-Komatsu on the promise that the two lines would alternate on the throne. The promise was never kept.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-go-kameyama.jpg" alt="Emperor Go-Kameyama" width="320" height="530" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Published by メディアックス(Mediax) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emperor_Go-Kameyama.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
